// The app's identity: the Apple team, the bundle id prefix, the app group and
// the keychain group. Every target derives its ids from these, so a fork can
// build and sign under its own Apple team by overriding them in Local.xcconfig
// (see Local.xcconfig.example and docs/development/local-build.md) without
// changing any source file.
//
// The app and its extensions read SWP_BUNDLE_ID_PREFIX and SWP_APP_GROUP at run
// time from their Info.plist (SWPBundleIDPrefix, SWPAppGroupIdentifier); see
// Common/Sources/Common/AppIdentity.swift, whose defaults must equal the values
// below (a test in CommonTests checks it).
//
// Included by Base.xcconfig (followed by the optional Local.xcconfig) and by
// scripts/CIArchiveSigning.xcconfig, which is passed with -xcconfig and so
// restores these values over any Local.xcconfig: an archive never picks up a
// local identity or team.

DEVELOPMENT_TEAM = ZHKJ4NHK6F

SWP_BUNDLE_ID_PREFIX = com.paulgessinger.swift-paperless
SWP_APP_GROUP = group.com.paulgessinger.swift-paperless
SWP_KEYCHAIN_GROUP = $(AppIdentifierPrefix)$(SWP_BUNDLE_ID_PREFIX)
